--
N5008 [stmt.ambig]/1 and [dcl.decl.general]: `T(x);', `int (i) = k;',
`int (*p) = &i;' are declarations.  For a type name the parser knows, rDeclarator
accepts the parenthesised declarator; for a name it does not (a nested class
declared later, [class.mem.general]/7) the type checker rewrites the
call-shaped expression statement into the declaration.
